<h2>The same ideas, natively, in OBS</h2>
<p><a href="https://github.com/imswarnil/Tally">Tally</a> is an OBS Studio plugin that draws this same set of sources — a tally light, a lower third, a ticker, a camera frame, a visualiser, a clock, a countdown, a card and a backdrop — inside OBS itself, in C against libobs, with no browser source and no URL to paste. Its light reads OBS's real streaming state, which a web page cannot.</p>
<p>The two are <strong>independent by design</strong>. Tally is MIT and public; this system is sold. Not a line of code crosses between them in either direction — what they share is a sensibility, and that is all they are allowed to share. Use the pages above when the overlay is a browser source or a screenshot, and Tally when it is a source in OBS's own <em>+</em> menu.</p>
